# Templ Frontend

Package: `frontend`. One page/feature per file (`students.templ`, `process.templ`).

## Page Structure

Full HTML with shared includes:

```templ
templ Students(data StudentData) {
	<!DOCTYPE html>
	<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<title>Students - Zion English Admin Tool</title>
		<link rel="icon" href={ utils.URL("/static/favicon.ico") }/>
		@GlobalIncludes()
	</head>
	<body>
		<div class="container">
			@HeaderSimple()
			// content
		</div>
	</body>
	</html>
}
```

## View vs API Structs

- Display structs (`StudentData`, `StudentItem`) → define in `.templ` file
- Form/API DTOs → `internal/models`; handlers map between them

## Shared Components

| Component | File |
|-----------|------|
| `@GlobalIncludes()` | `global.templ` |
| `@HeaderSimple()` | `header.templ` |
| `@TeacherDropdown()` | `dropdowns.templ` |
| `@ScrHTMX()` | `scripts.templ` |
| `@IconActionLink()` / `@IconActionButton()` | `icons.templ` — use `IconKind` constants, not string literals |
| `@Pill()` / `@StatusPill()` | `pills.templ` — use `PillTone` constants, not string literals |
| `@TeacherNameCell()` | `avatar.templ` — avatar + teacher name; use whenever a teacher name is shown |

## Pills

Use `@Pill` and `@StatusPill` from `pills.templ` for status and label badges. All pills share a black border via `--pill-border: 1px solid #000` in `global.templ` (applied to `.pill` and `.status-pill`).

- Do not override pill borders with softer `var(--color-border)` unless a design explicitly requires an exception.
- Custom pill-shaped UI (e.g. `.lm-tag-pill`, `.class-lm-readonly-pill`, `.class-lm-chip`) must use `border: var(--pill-border)` — do not hardcode border colors.
- Prefer extending `.pill` / `.status-pill` classes over inventing one-off pill styles.

## Teacher name display

Whenever a teacher name is shown in the UI, render it with `@TeacherNameCell(name, avatar)` from `avatar.templ` (or a list wrapper like `@EntityViewTeacherList`).

- Populate `AvatarProps` in handlers via `buildTeacherListAvatarProps` (or equivalent) — do not show bare name strings in tables, modals, or detail views.
- Include `@AvatarStyles()` on pages that render teacher names outside `GlobalIncludes` partials that already load avatar CSS.

## Icon actions

Action icon kinds are typed as `IconKind` in [`icon_kind.go`](icon_kind.go). Use `@IconActionLink`, `@IconActionButton`, and `@IconActionSubmit` with `IconKind` constants — never build action buttons in client-side JavaScript.

## SSR over client-side DOM building

Prefer server-side rendering with templ components and HTMX partial fetches over complex inline JavaScript.

**Do:**
- Render rows, lists, buttons, and icons in `.templ` (`@IconActionLink`, `@IconActionButton`, row/list components)
- Load dynamic UI via `hx-get` / `hx-post` to handlers that return HTML fragments (see `handleGetTeacherRow`, `/schedule/partials/list`, `/classes/partials/rows`, `/reports/partials/rows`)
- Map DB/API data to view structs in handlers; keep templates declarative
- Keep page JS minimal: calendar navigation, modal open/close/focus, delegated clicks on `data-*` attributes

**Avoid:**
- `fetch` + `JSON.parse` + `innerHTML` / `createElement` to assemble table rows or action buttons
- Embedding HTML/SVG in JSON for client-side assembly
- Global JS helpers that duplicate templ components (`createIconActionLink`, `window.actionIcons`, etc.)

**When JSON is still OK:** lightweight read-only data for widgets that genuinely need client-side state (e.g. calendar date→count summaries), not for markup that templ can render.

## URLs

Always use `utils.URL("/path")` — prepends `/zion-english-admin` in local dev.

## HTMX Forms

```templ
<form hx-post={ utils.URL("/process") } hx-target="#results" hx-swap="innerHTML">
```

Dropdowns load via HTMX on page load: `hx-get`, `hx-trigger="load"`, `hx-target="this"`.

## CSS

CSS variables in `:root` (`global.templ`). Page-specific styles in inline `<style>` blocks.

### Inline chip remove buttons

Global `button` styles in `global.templ` set `margin-top`, padding, `display: inline-block`, and filled backgrounds. Any small remove/close control inside a chip, tag, or pill **must** override those defaults or the × will sit below the label.

Use the same reset as `.lm-tag-chip-remove` in `learning_materials.templ`:

```css
.chip-remove {
	display: inline-flex;
	align-items: center;
	justify-content: center;
	width: 1.125rem;
	height: 1.125rem;
	padding: 0;
	margin: 0;
	margin-top: 0;
	border: none;
	border-radius: var(--radius-full);
	background: transparent;
	background-color: transparent;
	flex-shrink: 0;
	line-height: 1;
}
.chip-remove:hover {
	background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06);
	background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06);
}
```

Parent chip/tag container: `display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: …`.

When adding a new chip UI, copy this pattern — do not rely on bare `button { padding: 0 }` alone.
